#:seon.config.cache{:max-bytes [:int {:min 1 :seon.config/dial true :seon.config/default 512000000 :description "THE byte budget of the process cache (seon.cache): estimated bytes every derived value Seon keeps may weigh together, evicted by W-TinyLFU beyond it. About 5% of a 10.5 GB heap (cache-central design 2026-09-26). Datahike's node and query caches keep their own dials. The last cluster booted in a JVM applies its value to the process."}],
 :contract-table-capacity [:int {:min 1 :seon.config/dial true :seon.config/default 512 :description "How many compiled function contracts one schema population's table keeps (contracts-out-of-projection design §10, root ruling 2026-09-27). The population's process-cache entry is charged the population once plus this many slot charges and is evicted with its slots. Read by the acquisition owner and passed to seon.schema/retained-contract; no production caller until slice 4."}]}
